;">Tech dissection: datacenters divide Silicon Valley from US conservatives=
 (except Trump)</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Silicon Valley has underestimated the back=
lash to datacenters in the US by a country mile. That opposition has now ac=
hieved substantial political momentum: it=E2=80=99s blocking proposed proje=
cts, nixing tax and power incentives, tilting the balance of the upcoming U=
S elections.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The backlash has even led US conservatives=
 =E2=80=93 politicians and constituents =E2=80=93 to split from wealthy all=
ies in Silicon Valley.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The opposition to datacenters in the US ha=
s become so widespread that it is crossing partisan lines. Several prominen=
t US conservatives, including the governors of Texas and Florida, have cond=
emned datacenters=E2=80=99 enormous electricity usage. Both states=E2=80=99=
 governors hew closely to Trump on the majority of issues, but both have im=
plemented restrictions on datacenters=E2=80=99 access to their states=E2=80=
=99 power grids.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.thegua=
rdian.com/ss/c/u001.pukHoRYe7TiUOlF_IY_t7NyfOxtS4xgt0HdWbRQtOGhgzroEd8fBMJo=
WWGmVF1owOh3ttIhZE7EaDclFnisjo4IFj0qH6n6UtGX4KR5Py66q-xWYbCYi9uJmwNx699ThK2=
tvrTmGuazI8Tf9Ux5gOPT9Kw_GLj3h19wyfHiwlCAkKCdkoMleu1Vt2F1xvPVFSMrSK4_dpM_ii=
9afzb1imQGyWW2HmKgiDzd45EzQ7RX7jjpfPa598f17lBq5jbTsXniNkAZB7f3Uri14_KBLn44X=
elwmdooDcOVk8sivK7ISV1LcIes_yGOtBBT7yUX4C5qHWUAQVPlQ3vqlz8z9zg/4to/Myvj0_Q8=
T8SBLcFS8LXkeA/h26/h001.iK7jgftuvYvABDoB-1-IcRdPaPopn5nn3GwaU_GH1fc" style=
=3D"color: #0077B6;">All of the candidates</a> in the race to become Ohio=
=E2=80=99s next governor, including a member of Trump=E2=80=99s own adminis=
tration, have called for restrictions on new datacenters. Meanwhile, the li=
beral governor of New York has implemented a yearlong moratorium on new hyp=
er-scale datacenters.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Read more: <a href=3D"https://abli=
nk.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszc=
CSneHEDUZSC8KPzZutimV4n8d8SzVDLrKeyiGJj631BeGVdLBOmNOFZqM757b9M2insOk6FaXPH=
