Kzm7o5DHOo5m8agpEQW8Z3LniAMDIHVqxZZuF_fJ-yigaI1HSMnOQw64pQP/4to/Myvj0_Q8T8S=
BLcFS8LXkeA/h27/h001.2y_BtMfDk8fhYXbwmPBr8QmlkCdVWXzmxkO0w0d7YOY" style=3D"=
color: #0077B6;">The datacenter backlash is bringing the entire political s=
pectrum together =E2=80=93 against big tech billionaires</a></strong></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">How did the tech giants=E2=80=99 leaders s=
et themselves up so disastrously? AI CEOs have =E2=80=9Cfailed miserably=E2=
=80=9D to endear the public to their cause, noted Chamath Palihapitiya, a v=
enture capitalist and co-host of the Silicon Valley podcast All In, <a href=
=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.QvkQtXiSzSINXrMyEJiu=
Yj4DeghJb-Z4JzGlxFd_HGw9X024MCI9tKR09jtBFYFYkxBXpxXCviolEQG07Qcfs5Aa-rFaYKP=
rNtGnOt7N8X2th1M59oDJOKSsHYiKELxThOXk7vq72nrTxMATvyH-seYCXYOmsTYSa3UENLsdHt=
_fRAmf9gckPujhnMgGHnrDNr_wB80bHBeOStNl7BlXGGhxwtUS9Pg6kSRFh9TvHWHJ7B1nMIjil=
ciKHrCqNxHi/4to/Myvj0_Q8T8SBLcFS8LXkeA/h28/h001.rCLn2uUVJr2kwTB-DW-UeCExfOA=
FGIXnP5C3oSeDHP0" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">on X</a>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Executives such as Sam Altman and Dario Am=
odei have focused their attention on Trump, legislators, and other power pl=
ayers in their bids for huge investments. It turns out the public, uncourte=
d by AI executives, also has a say in whether the technology deserves so ma=
ny public resources.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Communities across the country are bristli=
ng at the emergence of the behemoths in their backyards. They=E2=80=99re ra=
ising questions about their impact on the environment, and the effect on th=
eir utility bills. But there=E2=80=99s more. Datacenters have become a stan=
d-in for grievances against technology companies =E2=80=93 harms to childre=
n, the feeling of too-rapid societal change with no opt-out, the loss of co=
ntrol over our attention, the extreme concentration of political and econom=
ic power in the hands of a few inhumane men =E2=80=93 and the tide of that =
resentment is rising.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99m not anti-datacenter. =
I=E2=80=99m anti-the people who run datacenters,=E2=80=9D Benny Johnson, a =
popular rightwing commentator on social media, said in response to Palihapi=
tiya, adding: =E2=80=9CI have critical policymakers on my live show daily. =
The Governor of Texas was on yesterday. I=E2=80=99ve received ZERO effort f=
rom anyone in the tech industry to even try to explain data centers=E2=80=
=A6=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Read more: <a href=3D"https://abli=
nk.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszc=
CSneHEAhzD0WUI17vwhqJTqDOvEGXsItKGeeuNhTu_20FxRpyGGMmNghrpOcTofm0as0yDP1At_=
mK63I_e-eI4VCY6Dro02qpH9eH4x6jM_YwST611xqScScR041k-8tVDTBN6XX1-ylLRUAivGS7A=
QpdHd1lp5-EI7Uwvc624tfkJ5ZfSYsN_x_l_eeSafH6YfzXh9NTO-ZmIE_kxhPj1-Seme2DsKXp=
