8T8SBLcFS8LXkeA/h49/h001.Hd3iIdJBtVNp7RHoS-6AozIXWCpW-Nlb_Sv_izoNBeg" style=
=3D"color: #0077B6;">Reworked series of stories on AI and work</a>, editor =
Danielle Abril will answer readers=E2=80=99 questions about the changing wo=
rkplace. You can ask a question for future editions by emailing us at <stro=
ng style=3D"color: #052962; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;"><a href=
=3D"mailto:techscape.us@theguardian.com?utm_term=3D6a96c2ad3c3272af4ff6403a=
6b08e950&amp;utm_campaign=3DTechScape&amp;utm_source=3Desp&amp;utm_medium=
=3DEmail&amp;CMP=3Dtechscape_email" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">techscape.us@=
theguardian.com</a></strong>.</em></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"></p>
<hr class=3D"dinkus" style=3D"border-color: #052962; border-width: 4px; bor=
der-style: solid; max-width: 280px; margin: 16px 0 10px;">
<br style=3D"display: none;"><em style=3D"font-size: 24px; line-height: 28p=
x; padding-bottom: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px;">This week, readers ask: what =
skills do I need to learn to stay employable as more companies adopt AI?</e=
m><p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">For workers whose jobs may be affected by =
AI, the takeaways from several studies all point to a somewhat counterintui=
tive answer: yes, you should familiarize yourself with generative AI tools.=
 But at least as important: sharpen your human skills. Judgment, adaptabili=
ty, analytical thinking and leadership all may become differentiators as AI=
 gets embedded in work.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Ask yourself: can you critically judge AI=
=E2=80=99s output? Can you quickly adapt to change? Can you problem-solve a=
nd delegate tasks efficiently to humans and AI?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CLearn to work with AI in your fie=
ld, while continuing to build the human and domain skills that help you app=
ly it well,=E2=80=9D said Elena Magrini, head of global research for labor =
market intelligence firm <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.co=
m/ss/c/u001.BcPF2cTaS3oq-3YoY-9Jinlp0wZ3nViiN25L5f7uPx0U5eynIQZoAZ1DckbNUq_=
6l7zGASFp4LDhP8P_xnt5uLVdXUu8Xr9WxuECi7P2JC_dzs8XB524BBDlBM_pdQBXNl_9p3txbn=
nJ7ml72XMgX67QljtrY1gPJVWMwAPcedtQYCEdWwt57ZLh6KQE0-8r/4to/Myvj0_Q8T8SBLcFS=
8LXkeA/h50/h001.7kOnbpn-5H2Lj5aCyF3z3DJ0vILc_GlnTEz-YmsZNHA" style=3D"color=
: #0077B6;">Lightcast.io</a>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The tasks that employers are adding to AI-=
exposed jobs often rely on human skills such as empathy, judgment and creat=
ivity, according to PwC=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.thegu=
ardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR_c2uW_wkLDWf2Ly6M0tqYSUR4CTi36Rp6=
YKx1nL5zjOp7oKNaUGs-GGMZVkFskZnhzBE4_6dFKY8gLqeU9LL5IhP9IIbXQSrvVcnDKgvgaED=
JbPkonHm_nfDtsWZHxz1DtJQdnc6aUFxMEk9gjnpQ3QRdFT33O0Z3mDAhJPbxi9zvfULi9sqfN3=
4pgv9tH8cltgFxT5cJwigSi0Sq0Xcw93piRlw1u7Ivql-FZeKUY-a5fZgWI5JNi7h7d6dry505E=
uwukHUubuCnw4ia65BcAP6inX8_Yh0tapJ1uTHYhwYbktboz1QpRuhsIYb296sA/4to/Myvj0_Q=
8T8SBLcFS8LXkeA/h51/h001.uwcnmAmduRSeBo4vMZK2IBxxmyA1AvlM0Ntx4FCA5fk" style=
=3D"color: #0077B6;">2026 Global AI Jobs Barometer report</a>, which is bas=
ed on 1bn job ads from six continents. Junior roles are now more likely to =
require traditionally senior skills like emotional intelligence and leaders=
hip, the report stated. In LinkedIn=E2=80=99s 2026 Skills on the Rise repor=
t, based on skills members added to their profiles along with those held by=
 recent hires, in-demand skills included team management, cross-functional =
collaboration and mentorship, as well as prompt engineering and AI business=
 strategy.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">One way to start developing experience in =
leadership and problem solving is at your own company. Work with your boss =
to find internal training and mentorship programs. And consider volunteerin=
g for tasks that may allow you to boost your weaker skills like leading a c=
ross-functional project that requires you to delegate and communicate often=
. Beyond your employer, companies such as LinkedIn and Coursera offer free =
online courses for soft and technical skills and OpenAI and Anthropic provi=
de educational materials on how to use AI.</p>
